  "number": "5.11.3",
  "title": "",
  "body": "  What is printed by this program?   #include <iostream> struct Rectangle { double length; double width; }; double calculate_area(const Rectangle& rectangle) { return rectangle.length * rectangle.width; } int main() { Rectangle rectangle{5.0, 2.0}; std::cout << calculate_area(rectangle) << '\\n'; }      5.0  The function multiplies both members; it does not return only the length.    2.0  The function multiplies both members; it does not return only the width.    10.0  Correct. The area is 5.0 * 2.0 .    25.0  The expression multiplies length by width, not length by itself.    "
