  "number": "5.11.4",
  "title": "",
  "body": "  Which parameter form is most appropriate for a function that only reads a large object?     Rectangle rectangle  This passes a copy, which may be unnecessary when the function only reads the object.    Rectangle& rectangle  A non-const reference allows modification, which is not needed for a read-only function.    const Rectangle& rectangle  Correct. This avoids a copy and prevents the function from modifying the argument.    const Rectangle rectangle&  The ampersand belongs before the parameter name: const Rectangle& rectangle .    "
