  "type": "Exercise",
  "number": "5.11.6",
  "title": "",
  "body": "  What does const at the end of this member-function declaration mean?   double get_balance() const;      The return value cannot be a double .  The return type is still double ; the trailing const applies to the member function.    The function promises not to change the object's state.  Correct. A const member function can observe the object but cannot normally modify its data members.    The function can only be called from inside the class.  const does not control public or private access.    The object must be declared with the keyword const .  Const objects require const member functions, but a const member function can also be called on a non-const object.    "
